# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored here: consumers pull this package as a git
# dep and Vite does not transpile dependencies, so the built ESM + .d.ts must be
# committed in the tag. See README.md. The repo root ignores `dist/` globally,
# so this un-ignores it for this subtree only — without it, `git add web_ui`
# silently skips the build and the tag ships a package with no code in it.
!dist/
!dist/**
node_modules/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
